<title>BELGIUM: EU beef market rising slightly says Commission.</title>
<headline>EU beef market rising slightly says Commission.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beef sales in the European Union appear to have stabilised and are rising slightly, an EU official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The amount of beef offered for intervention at this week's EU beef management committee was unexpectedly low. The market appears to have bottomed out and is rising slightly,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The beef management committee accepted tenders for 20,900 tonnes of beef from offers of 34,000 tonnes at a minimum price of 235 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
</text>
